SUMMARY:2nd Friday ArtWalk: Acktoberfest
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Ackland Art Museum’s fifth annual Acktoberfest — an evening filled with art\, crafts\, and local vendors! \nArt supplies will be available in our ART& space\, where visitors can create their own paper plants inspired by Phaan Howng: Against Nature. There will also be postcards inspired by the installation for visitors to enjoy and use. \nExplore our special exhibitions Care and Concern: Recent Acquisitions of Modern and Contemporary Art \, and Continental Shift: Recent Acquisitions of African Art throughout the evening with extended museum hours. \nLocal vendors will be on hand with goods to browse and purchase\, including Dingo Dog Brewing Company\, where visitors can grab a drink to sip while crafting. \nA full list of vendors will be published closer to the event date. \nAcktoberfest is a free\, walk-in program; no registration required to attend or craft. Museum galleries will be open from 5–9 p.m.; the vendors will be onsite from 6–8:30 p.m.
URL:https://events.ackland.org/event/2nd-friday-artwalk-acktoberfest/
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum\, 101 S. Columbia Street\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:2nd Friday ArtWalk,Special Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.ackland.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Ack-poster-scaled-e1788886283117.png
END:VEVENT
